    "source_review_state_meaning": "Accepted means acceptance of this documented discrepancy diagnosis. It does not mean acceptance of the formalization as an exact rendering of the pinned source, acceptance of a corrected source, or approval of any repair.",
    "review_evidence": "This review used only the designated anti-anchored packet. I did not inspect repository instructions, implementation bodies, prior reviews, repair suggestions, other agents' work, or external sources. Independence here means that the reviewer is distinct from the stated formalizer and blind decoder and assessed the supplied source evidence against their supplied artifacts independently.\n\nThe decisive finding is a direct mathematical counterexample on the finite Boolean domain itself. Let V = {0,1}, select v = 0, take x = (0,1), and let μ assign mass 1/4 to every configuration. Conditioning on the old complementary coordinate gives F_x = {(0,1),(1,1)} of mass 1/2. The reconstructed law is uniform on this fiber. The literal source instructions instead set the next second coordinate to x_0 = 0 and sample the first coordinate uniformly, yielding a law on {(0,0),(1,0)}. Thus the two laws differ even when every reconstructed assumption is satisfied. The selected-coordinate conditional marginal is compatible in this example; the nonselected-coordinate assignment is not.\n\nThe instruction pair suggests a possible indexing error in the pinned step 2, because step 3 conditions on old complementary values whereas step 2 overwrites those values with the old selected value. Nevertheless, the available evidence does not establish whether the published PDF contains that error, whether the packet excerpt is inaccurate, or whether omitted context changes its interpretation. Consequently, possible-source-error is a diagnosis of the supplied source representation, not a verified erratum to the publication.\n\nIndependently, positive complementary-fiber mass is a genuine qualification. It would follow from μ({x}) > 0 in the finite model, but the packet does not state that Ω is precisely positive-probability support or that the current state has positive mass. The source's conditional-law instruction therefore remains underspecified at null conditioning events relative to the explicit theorem premise. I cannot classify this premise as merely an exposed source-implicit assumption on the evidence provided.\n\nThe generalized measure-theoretic setting can contain the usual finite Boolean specialization, with the source measure embedded in an ambient product and the relevant measurability assumptions supplied. This gives a plausible relationship between the mathematical constructions but does not erase the literal assignment discrepancy, prove the source's unstated support assumptions, or make the generalization an exact source statement.\n\nThe packet reports that the Lean statement compiled. I have not independently checked compilation, the proof, or the definition of CoordinateHeatBath.heatBath. Its conditional-kernel interpretation is supplied by the blind reconstruction and is not recoverable in full from the opaque declaration name alone. Accordingly, conclusions about that implementation are conditional on the supplied reconstruction accurately describing it.\n\nThe source evidence consists of two short excerpts plus an explicitly nonquoted context paraphrase. This limits conclusions about the surrounding publication and prevents verification of source transcription or broader conventions. The reviewer_packet_sha256 value is copied from the packet's provided packet_sha256 field; I did not produce or independently verify a packet hash. review_run_sha256 is intentionally empty for the root to populate by hashing the immutable returned record. No repair is approved."
